#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
Standalone portable industry input pipeline for H2RES.

Orchestrates the existing industry workflow:
1) allocate NUTS x sector x fuel x temperature-bin annual demand from JRC-IDEES
2) generate industrial technology tables and hourly demand distributions
3) split chemical non-energy/feedstock demand into explicit non_energy_* rows

Default outputs:
  - industry_units_by_category_ALL_NON_ENERGY.csv
  - industry_hourly_distributions_by_category_ALL_NON_ENERGY.csv

Copy only this file to another computer and run it. Embedded helper scripts
are extracted to .industry_pipeline_helpers on first run. Large public
datasets are cached under ./data by default. EU ETS installation/compliance
tables and EEA industrial-site records are downloaded automatically. Sector
activity at installation coordinates determines regional shares. Equal shares
require an explicit --regional-allocation equal assumption.
"""

